ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/physicsvigilante/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Draft M37a — new JEE-relevant grounded-wire-current observable\n\n**Frozen charter BEFORE code:** `docs/m37a_charter.md` committed at `89dae06df53403a8fab6743ad8bdcc10fc76c514`.\n**Released base:** M36e merge `dc347251c14e449c53d51820b4481d1bfbee2cfb`, Git tree `60b4f21aa88a2031ec50c5d1e7c15a5135a7becf`, 20/20 real main-push CI passed.\n\nM37a adds **a new ideal quasistatic ground-wire current observer**, not a new 3D electrostatic solver or fake motion animation. Existing exact Kelvin ground-sphere and M13 force/energy are observed at each source position. A teacher-supplied instantaneous velocity gives only `I_sphere→ground=-q a v_radial/d²` (conventional positive-charge direction); true radial `I(t)` consumes actual M16a trajectories, verifies the full timeline against fresh M16a integration, and retains real elapsed time, energy, guard and source model. Signed induced charge `Q_sphere=-q a/d` is derived from the native physical solution. No wire resistance, EM delay, radiation or surface-contact dynamics.\n\n**Novel evidence:** independent SI force `F_r=-k q² a d/(d²-a²)²`, mechanical energy `U=-k q² a/[2(d²-a²)]`, native-position charge derivative `-dQ/dt`; positive/negative incoming/outgoing/tangential, translated and rotated geometry, permittivity, actual RK4 radial time series, near-surface guard, hostile false sign/charge/velocity/energy/time/provenance refusals. Independent stdlib JSON physics checker imports **no conductor_sim**. Dedicated Python 3.10/3.12 workflow plus full inherited CI required.\n\n**JEE fidelity:** the M36a audit lists physical p8 Multiple Correct Q21 in `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` as partial. No unreviewed claim of the problem's complete source wording/answer or numeric givens; this PR is a reusable *current observable* first. Original source page and answer need independent visual inspection in review.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE OR MARK READY** until current exact-head source CI (full Python 3.10/3.12, historical browser, real FEMM 5, new M37a physics), new fresh independent source-pinned reviewer math/browser-source checks, explicit owner authorization, exact-head merge and postmerge main-push CI. Unrelated physics/solver/renderer files remain unchanged.\n\nSee [M37a charter](docs/m37a_charter.md), [design + limits](docs/m37a.md), `src/conductor_sim/grounded_sphere_wire.py`, `tests/test_m37a_grounded_wire_current.py`, `tools/m37a_ground_wire_reference.py`, and `examples/grounded_sphere_wire_current.py`.\n\n### Independent review #01 — historically CHANGES REQUESTED; correction candidate #02\n\n[Independent review #01](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/review/conductor-pr89-chat-b-20261118/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/reviews/review-01-chat-b.md) executed **73 reviewer-authored cases** at the OLD source `75c984aaae18e44997332e330ed3a519a7b6a8da` / Git tree `e1dbb9bb673f4efc2950939d0c1e021697393d59`. Physics+Kelvin force/energy+signed wire current and four real M16a histories passed; the independent first workflow [#44307096311](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/actions/runs/44307096311) **FAILED deliberately** on **11 unexpected acceptances**: F1 Boolean charge/radius/permittivity, F2 missing/false SI unit declarations, F3 false trace method/mode/current-sign or changing conductor identity. Never relabel this old review PASS.\n\nCurrent corrected source SHA: **`adfe9098742c663e9f4132c3e29e86dddf7ecc1e`**; actual native Git TREE **`43f8ebae4937eacc25143fdace324115edcfb2d0`**. Corrections affect **only** new M37a observer strict scalar boundary, separate stdlib SI checker, and targeted regression tests; all historical solver, M16 integrator, FEMM, generic renderer and PDFs untouched.\n- **F1:** reject Boolean dimensional Q, sphere R and epsilon before Kelvin solve; preserve actual q sign and positive radius/permittivity.\n- **F2:** require complete exact instantaneous and M16a physical SI-unit declarations. Reject mA/eV/ms and missing/contradictory maps without silently converting numbers.\n- **F3:** require fixed name/centre/R/epsilon throughout trace, correct actual M16a method/mode, conventional terminal-current direction and truthful quasistatic interpretation.\n- **Developer-controlled corrected focused CI:** 118 tests passed each on Python 3.10 and 3.12, genuine example generation and separate no-production-import SI JSON check. **Full exact-head PR+branch-push CI must finish green**; pending checks are not a PASS.\n- **Fresh independent R2 pending:** [REQUEST #02](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REQUEST-02.md) and [REVIEWER PROMPT #02](https://github.com/physicsvigilante/review_sandbox/blob/main/projects/conductor_sim/pr-89/REVIEWER-PROMPT-02.md). Re-run original attacks, new hostile mutations, actual SI math and real elapsed-time integrity on the EXACT new HEAD/TREE.\n\n**Source educational boundary:** independent reviewer visually inspected the ORIGINAL workbook `02_conductors_half_size.pdf` physical p8 Multiple Correct Q21 and physical p17 answer key. The printed positive charge approaches the grounded sphere at **prescribed constant small speed**, giving conventional sphere→ground current `+qRv/d²`, which **increases** as d shrinks; printed correct options **(1),(3)**. This is distinct from an unforced accelerating M16a charge, and teacher numbers are not original source givens. M37a still does not claim a source-specific machine-scored whole-question simulation or current-graph browser.\n\n**PR #89 STAYS DRAFT AND UNMERGED. NO OWNER MERGE APPROVAL OR NEW INDEPENDENT PASS.** Any successful independent review requires a separate explicit owner merge decision, exact-head guarded merge and postmerge real main-push CI.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T12:21:06Z","updated_a